WEBVTT

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.836
Captain's Log,
Stardate 44769.2.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:09.137
For some weeks we have had
a Klingon exobiologist on board

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.541
as part of a scientific
exchange program.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.170
Unfortunately, we suspect

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.875
that he was involved
in a security breach

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.975
and in the possible sabotage
of our warp drive.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:22.477
What were you doing accessing
the propulsion system files

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.648
on stardate 44758?

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.987
I didn't.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.654
Yes, you did, from
computer 12B9, deck 36.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.753
The computer logged in

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.923
your identification
from your communicator.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.398
It must be a mistake.

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:36.402
J'Dan,
we have confirmed reports

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.928
that schematic drawings
of our dilithium chamber

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.942
fell into Romulan hands
one week later.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.000
I know nothing about it.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.442
I suppose you know

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.776
nothing about the explosion
that disabled the warp drive

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:48.974
approximately the same time.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:50.983
No, I was not involved.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.451
You accuse me
because I am Klingon.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:58.519
Our Chief of Security
is Klingon.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.526
That has nothing to do with it.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.290
Send me home then
if you are so distrusting.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.923
We've already contacted
the Klingon High Council.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.193
You'll be returned home

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.326
as soon as we finish
our investigation.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.337
I have nothing more to say.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.736
Very well.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:16.037
Worf, accompany the Lieutenant
to his quarters.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.084
What do you think?

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:29.088
It's hard to tell.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:33.456
He's very closed,
but he is hiding something.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:40.188
On the Klingon Homeworld,
your name is not mentioned.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:43.999
It is as though
you never existed.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:47.495
A terrible burden
for a warrior to bear...

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.337
to become nothing

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.343
to be without honor

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:54.039
without the chance for glory.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.017
I have friends...

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:04.956
powerful friends
on the homeworld.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.959
I could talk to them.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.962
They might help
to restore your name...

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:13.989
if you could just take me
to a shuttlecraft.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:22.998
It could be done
without anyone knowing about it.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.510
I don't know how you transferred

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.482
secret information
to the Romulans

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.711
but I will find out!

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:32.718
Pahtk!

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:35.880
And when we inform
the Klingon High Council

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.447
they will put you
to a slow death.

00:03:14.826 --> 00:03:19.229
Space, the final frontier.

00:03:19.264 --> 00:03:23.098
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:25.103
Its continuing mission...

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:29.073
to explore strange new worlds

00:03:29.107 --> 00:03:33.544
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:03:33.578 --> 00:03:38.072
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.138
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:04:38.176 --> 00:04:39.871
Retired Admiral Norah Satie

00:04:39.911 --> 00:04:42.903
whose investigation exposed
the alien conspiracy

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:46.349
against Starfleet Command
three years ago, is arriving

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:48.012
to assist in our inquiry.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:53.421
Captain Picard.

00:04:53.458 --> 00:04:56.689
Admiral Satie,
welcome aboard the Enterprise.

00:04:56.728 --> 00:04:58.355
Delighted to be here.

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.365
I managed to acquire
my former staff.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.367
My aide, Sabin Genestra,

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:03.868
from Betazed

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:07.201
and my assistant,
Nellen Tore, from Delb II.

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:09.104
This is my First Officer

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:10.608
Commander William Riker.

00:05:10.642 --> 00:05:13.110
May I show you to your quarters?

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:14.612
Captain, if Starfleet Command

00:05:14.646 --> 00:05:16.614
was so concerned
with your report

00:05:16.648 --> 00:05:18.616
they brought me
out of retirement

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.447
I think I should
get right to work.

00:05:20.485 --> 00:05:21.782
Very well.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.789
Commander Riker, will you
see to the Admiral's staff?

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:28.816
First, I'd like to inspect
the damage to your engine room.

00:05:33.498 --> 00:05:36.126
Admiral Satie,
this is Commander Data.

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:37.294
Commander La Forge.

00:05:37.335 --> 00:05:39.064
Admiral.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:40.662
We still can't
get in there, Captain.

00:05:40.705 --> 00:05:42.138
The radiation levels
are dropping

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:44.734
but they're still too high
to raise the isolation door.

00:05:44.776 --> 00:05:46.744
How much longer will it be?

00:05:46.778 --> 00:05:48.609
At the rate the levels
are decreasing

00:05:48.647 --> 00:05:50.672
we will gain entry
in 49 hours, Captain.

00:05:50.715 --> 00:05:52.205
Maybe the Admiral
would like to see

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.649
the visual log of the explosion?

00:05:53.685 --> 00:05:54.674
Yes.

00:06:03.628 --> 00:06:07.257
This was logged four days ago
at 0300 hours.

00:06:14.905 --> 00:06:17.897
At that point, the emergency
confinement field was activated

00:06:17.942 --> 00:06:19.637
and the isolation doors
came down.

00:06:19.677 --> 00:06:20.644
No one was killed

00:06:20.678 --> 00:06:22.270
but I have two people
in Sick Bay

00:06:22.313 --> 00:06:23.280
from radiation burns.

00:06:23.314 --> 00:06:25.612
Have you been able
to make any assessments?

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.948
A slow-motion study
of the explosion

00:06:27.985 --> 00:06:30.954
suggests that the articulation
frame collapsed.

00:06:30.988 --> 00:06:34.515
The schematics that were stolen
from the Enterprise...

00:06:34.558 --> 00:06:37.186
I believe some involved
the articulation frame

00:06:37.228 --> 00:06:38.752
of the dilithium chamber.

00:06:38.796 --> 00:06:41.788
That's one reason
we tend to suspect sabotage.

00:06:41.832 --> 00:06:44.801
Other evidence lends credence
to that theory, Captain.

00:06:44.835 --> 00:06:46.769
A review of the sensor logs
indicates

00:06:46.804 --> 00:06:48.271
that every system's reading

00:06:48.305 --> 00:06:49.966
was well
within normal parameters

00:06:50.074 --> 00:06:52.269
until 52 milliseconds
before the explosion.

00:06:52.309 --> 00:06:53.936
We haven't found anything

00:06:53.978 --> 00:06:55.309
that suggests
there was a malfunction

00:06:55.346 --> 00:06:56.506
anywhere along the line.

00:06:56.547 --> 00:06:59.948
Captain, I think I'm going
to need a full briefing

00:06:59.984 --> 00:07:01.747
before we go any further.

00:07:01.786 --> 00:07:03.151
By all means, Admiral.

00:07:05.656 --> 00:07:08.124
Commander Data

00:07:08.159 --> 00:07:09.592
La Forge

00:07:09.627 --> 00:07:12.255
I don't envy you your job.

00:07:12.296 --> 00:07:14.264
Good luck.

00:07:19.804 --> 00:07:21.829
There are
very disturbing overtones

00:07:21.872 --> 00:07:23.339
in the idea of a Klingon

00:07:23.374 --> 00:07:25.638
providing information
to the Romulans.

00:07:25.676 --> 00:07:29.305
Are you aware of any other
Klingon-Romulan connection

00:07:29.346 --> 00:07:32.577
that Starfleet
might have encountered recently?

00:07:32.616 --> 00:07:35.312
I don't believe...

00:07:35.352 --> 00:07:38.651
What Starfleet Command
knows or doesn't know

00:07:38.689 --> 00:07:40.589
is for me to reveal.

00:07:42.059 --> 00:07:48.089
Well, this ship has encountered
several incidents

00:07:48.132 --> 00:07:50.225
which might suggest
a potential alliance

00:07:50.267 --> 00:07:51.632
between those two powers.

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:53.637
We're well aware of that,
Captain.

00:07:53.671 --> 00:07:56.936
What we must concentrate on
is the business at hand.

00:07:58.142 --> 00:07:59.131
Come.

00:08:01.746 --> 00:08:02.906
Excuse me, Captain.

00:08:02.947 --> 00:08:04.312
I did not know that...

00:08:04.348 --> 00:08:05.713
Oh, please, Mr. Worf, come in.

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.911
I particularly want
my guest to meet you.

00:08:07.952 --> 00:08:10.250
Admiral Satie,
this is my Head of Security

00:08:10.287 --> 00:08:11.618
Lieutenant Worf.

00:08:11.655 --> 00:08:13.145
Captain, I have been pursuing

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:15.215
the investigation
of Lieutenant J'Dan.

00:08:15.259 --> 00:08:17.784
I believe I know
how he transferred information

00:08:17.828 --> 00:08:19.227
off the Enterprise.

00:08:19.263 --> 00:08:21.163
Well done, Lieutenant.

00:08:21.198 --> 00:08:23.462
This is J'Dan's...

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:27.335
a hyposyringe he uses to treat
his Ba'Itmasor Syndrome

00:08:27.371 --> 00:08:30.340
but this has been fitted
with an optical reader

00:08:30.374 --> 00:08:33.832
specially modified to read data
from Starfleet isolinear chips.

00:08:33.878 --> 00:08:36.506
He can extract digital
information from a computer

00:08:36.547 --> 00:08:39.141
encode it in the form
of amino acid sequences

00:08:39.183 --> 00:08:42.516
and transfer those sequences
into a fluid in the syringe.

00:08:42.553 --> 00:08:44.680
Then he injects someone

00:08:44.722 --> 00:08:46.952
perhaps even without
their knowledge.

00:08:47.057 --> 00:08:49.184
Or perhaps with their knowledge.

00:08:49.226 --> 00:08:51.888
The information would be carried
in their bloodstream

00:08:51.929 --> 00:08:53.453
in the form of inert proteins.

00:08:53.497 --> 00:08:57.763
The body itself becomes a
conveyor of top secret files.

00:08:59.837 --> 00:09:03.796
Lieutenant Worf,
when we confront J'Dan

00:09:03.841 --> 00:09:06.571
I want you to conduct
the interrogation.

00:09:08.946 --> 00:09:10.914
I would be honored.

00:09:10.948 --> 00:09:12.245
Captain.

00:09:12.283 --> 00:09:13.614
Admiral.

00:09:17.021 --> 00:09:19.922
Captain, I predict that officer

00:09:20.024 --> 00:09:23.790
will be extremely valuable
in this investigation.

00:09:27.832 --> 00:09:30.062
I have tracked the movements
of every person

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.830
who has left the Enterprise
since you have been here.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:36.931
I traced one Tarkanian diplomat
as far as the Cruses system

00:09:37.041 --> 00:09:40.909
where he disappeared,
and has not been seen since.

00:09:40.945 --> 00:09:42.936
That proves nothing.

00:09:47.151 --> 00:09:52.248
A hyposyringe was discovered
in your quarters.

00:09:52.289 --> 00:09:53.620
I take injections.

00:09:53.657 --> 00:09:55.090
Everyone knows that.

00:09:55.125 --> 00:09:57.423
But your injections
do not include

00:09:57.461 --> 00:09:59.088
an optical chip reader.

00:09:59.129 --> 00:10:01.757
This device has
but one function...

00:10:01.799 --> 00:10:04.962
to transform
computer information

00:10:05.002 --> 00:10:07.163
into biological sequences.

00:10:07.204 --> 00:10:10.071
The blood of all Klingons
has become water!

00:10:10.107 --> 00:10:11.734
Since the Federation Alliance

00:10:11.775 --> 00:10:14.744
we are turned into a nation
of mewling babies.

00:10:14.778 --> 00:10:16.575
The Romulans are strong.

00:10:16.614 --> 00:10:17.945
They are worthy allies.

00:10:17.982 --> 00:10:20.951
They do not turn Klingons
into weaklings, like you.

00:10:20.985 --> 00:10:22.953
Lieutenant...

00:10:26.657 --> 00:10:31.117
How did you damage
the dilithium chamber?

00:10:31.161 --> 00:10:32.492
I had nothing to do with that.

00:10:32.529 --> 00:10:33.996
You mean,
it was sheer coincidence

00:10:34.064 --> 00:10:37.864
that it was sabotaged after you
gave the plans for the design

00:10:37.902 --> 00:10:38.926
to the Romulans?

00:10:38.969 --> 00:10:41.301
I do not know.
I had nothing to do with it.

00:10:41.338 --> 00:10:43.272
You've admitted your crime.

00:10:43.307 --> 00:10:45.275
Why lie now?

00:10:45.309 --> 00:10:47.504
I am not lying.

00:10:50.681 --> 00:10:53.878
Mr. Worf,
you may have him confined.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:04.827
Sabin?

00:11:04.862 --> 00:11:07.490
I believe
he's telling the truth.

00:11:07.531 --> 00:11:08.964
He admits stealing the files

00:11:09.066 --> 00:11:11.261
but not sabotaging
the dilithium chamber.

00:11:11.302 --> 00:11:14.100
I get no sense that he's lying.

00:11:14.138 --> 00:11:17.733
But if you're right,
someone else may be involved.

00:11:17.775 --> 00:11:19.140
I think, Captain

00:11:19.176 --> 00:11:22.145
you have a bigger problem
on your ship

00:11:22.179 --> 00:11:24.670
than just one
Klingon exchange officer.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:42.130
I've seen this before.

00:11:42.166 --> 00:11:44.634
A specter of conspiracy
on a starship

00:11:44.668 --> 00:11:46.499
is a frightening one.

00:11:46.537 --> 00:11:49.631
I can scarcely
believe it myself.

00:11:49.673 --> 00:11:53.200
But I am so grateful
for your presence, Admiral.

00:11:53.243 --> 00:11:56.542
If anyone in Starfleet
can help us, it's you.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:58.673
Captain...

00:11:58.716 --> 00:12:01.776
I find myself changing
my mind about you.

00:12:01.819 --> 00:12:02.979
In what way?

00:12:04.822 --> 00:12:08.883
When Starfleet ordered me here,
it was with the express command

00:12:08.926 --> 00:12:12.225
that we work together
on this problem as equals.

00:12:12.262 --> 00:12:15.527
My father taught me
to avoid partnerships.

00:12:15.566 --> 00:12:17.864
Most of them
are woefully lopsided.

00:12:17.901 --> 00:12:20.802
That sounds like
Judge Aaron Satie.

00:12:20.838 --> 00:12:22.635
You knew my father?

00:12:22.673 --> 00:12:23.970
Only from his writings.

00:12:24.041 --> 00:12:26.669
His judgments were
required reading at the Academy.

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:30.202
He was an extraordinary man.

00:12:33.017 --> 00:12:34.917
Every night at the dinner table

00:12:34.952 --> 00:12:37.512
he would pose
a question for debate.

00:12:37.554 --> 00:12:39.784
My big brothers and I
would wrangle it around

00:12:39.823 --> 00:12:41.791
from one side and the other.

00:12:41.825 --> 00:12:43.292
Father would referee.

00:12:43.327 --> 00:12:44.988
And he kept a stopwatch on us

00:12:45.062 --> 00:12:46.996
so we would have to learn
brevity

00:12:47.031 --> 00:12:48.692
but he wouldn't let us leave

00:12:48.732 --> 00:12:51.792
until he thought we'd completely
explored the issue.

00:12:51.835 --> 00:12:54.201
I'm willing to wager that you
trounced your brothers

00:12:54.238 --> 00:12:55.364
during those debates.

00:12:55.406 --> 00:12:57.135
More than once.

00:12:57.174 --> 00:13:00.337
Father loved it
when I nailed one of them

00:13:00.377 --> 00:13:02.504
with some subtle point of logic.

00:13:06.283 --> 00:13:09.351
All that I am, I owe to him.

00:13:09.484 --> 00:13:12.214
He was a giant.

00:13:12.253 --> 00:13:14.915
You must miss him very much.

00:13:14.956 --> 00:13:19.359
Captain, I always preferred
working alone.

00:13:19.394 --> 00:13:21.521
That way,
if something went wrong

00:13:21.563 --> 00:13:25.055
I didn't have to go far
for the cause.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:27.568
I resented you
being assigned to me

00:13:27.602 --> 00:13:29.661
but I was wrong.

00:13:29.704 --> 00:13:32.537
We're going to be quite a team.

00:13:34.843 --> 00:13:38.210
J'Dan did not make friends
easily.

00:13:38.246 --> 00:13:40.874
There are not many to question.

00:13:40.915 --> 00:13:43.440
You've done
a thorough job, Lieutenant.

00:13:43.485 --> 00:13:45.919
I am strongly motivated
in this matter.

00:13:45.954 --> 00:13:47.353
Yes, I can see that.

00:13:49.023 --> 00:13:51.958
I don't mind telling you,
I'm surprised.

00:13:51.993 --> 00:13:55.292
Frankly, when I first
heard about your father...

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.389
My father?

00:13:57.432 --> 00:13:59.195
Yes.

00:13:59.234 --> 00:14:00.599
There are some who believe

00:14:00.635 --> 00:14:02.762
he betrayed your people
to the Romulans.

00:14:02.804 --> 00:14:06.262
What he did or did not do
is no one's concern but my own.

00:14:06.307 --> 00:14:07.672
Of course.

00:14:07.709 --> 00:14:09.870
I only meant,
before I saw you in action

00:14:09.911 --> 00:14:13.176
I naturally considered you
to be a possible security risk.

00:14:13.214 --> 00:14:14.374
But I want you to know

00:14:14.416 --> 00:14:17.112
you have the Admiral's
and my complete confidence.

00:14:17.152 --> 00:14:19.882
You have nothing to prove to us.

00:14:19.921 --> 00:14:22.389
If there is
a conspiracy on board

00:14:22.424 --> 00:14:24.289
I promise you, I will find it.

00:14:24.325 --> 00:14:25.349
Good.

00:14:25.393 --> 00:14:27.759
You know the ship,
you know the personnel.

00:14:27.796 --> 00:14:29.957
You know exactly
what we're up against.

00:14:29.998 --> 00:14:32.432
We're counting on you,
Lieutenant.

00:14:32.467 --> 00:14:35.959
I will arrange
for the interviews to begin.

00:14:39.574 --> 00:14:41.667
And how often did
Lieutenant J'Dan

00:14:41.709 --> 00:14:43.438
come in for his injections?

00:14:43.478 --> 00:14:44.877
About once a week.

00:14:44.913 --> 00:14:46.813
Did you administer them
yourself?

00:14:46.848 --> 00:14:47.815
No.

00:14:47.849 --> 00:14:49.180
Well, who did?

00:14:49.217 --> 00:14:51.651
I had
one of my assistants do that.

00:14:51.686 --> 00:14:53.210
Did you ever hear
him say anything...

00:14:53.254 --> 00:14:55.552
anything that may have seemed
innocent at the time...

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:57.922
that might now shed some light
on this investigation?

00:14:57.959 --> 00:14:59.927
No. Nothing.

00:14:59.961 --> 00:15:02.759
In fact, he rarely spoke at all.

00:15:02.797 --> 00:15:03.923
Thank you, Dr. Crusher.

00:15:03.998 --> 00:15:05.829
We appreciate your time.
You're excused.

00:15:05.867 --> 00:15:08.131
Mr. Worf, will you
bring in the next person?

00:15:16.377 --> 00:15:19.938
Please sit down, Mr. Tarses.

00:15:20.048 --> 00:15:23.711
For the record, will you tell us
your name and position?

00:15:23.751 --> 00:15:25.116
Simon Tarses

00:15:25.153 --> 00:15:27.246
Crewman First Class,
Medical Technician.

00:15:27.288 --> 00:15:31.486
Now, I assure you, Mr. Tarses,
this is an informal inquiry.

00:15:31.526 --> 00:15:34.086
We are not accusing
you of anything.

00:15:34.128 --> 00:15:36.460
However, if you
would like counsel

00:15:36.498 --> 00:15:38.261
it can be provided.

00:15:38.299 --> 00:15:40.699
No, sir, I have nothing to hide.

00:15:40.735 --> 00:15:42.293
Tell me, how long have you held

00:15:42.337 --> 00:15:44.168
your appointment
aboard this vessel?

00:15:44.205 --> 00:15:47.106
Since Stardate 43587.

00:15:47.141 --> 00:15:49.575
Mr. Tarses, your records state

00:15:49.611 --> 00:15:52.171
that you were born
on Mars Colony.

00:15:52.213 --> 00:15:53.646
That's right.

00:15:53.681 --> 00:15:55.171
Then you are human?

00:15:55.216 --> 00:15:56.979
Largely.

00:15:57.018 --> 00:15:58.986
My paternal grandfather
was Vulcan.

00:15:59.087 --> 00:16:00.748
Yes, I see that.

00:16:00.788 --> 00:16:02.881
Tell me, what is
your relationship

00:16:02.924 --> 00:16:04.357
with the Klingon, J'Dan?

00:16:04.392 --> 00:16:07.054
Um, he...

00:16:07.095 --> 00:16:09.495
I mean, there's no relationship.

00:16:09.531 --> 00:16:11.897
He just came in
for his injections.

00:16:11.933 --> 00:16:14.128
Did you give him
those injections?

00:16:14.168 --> 00:16:15.362
Sometimes.

00:16:15.403 --> 00:16:17.928
There were several of us,
actually.

00:16:17.972 --> 00:16:20.463
I-I might ha-have done it twice.

00:16:20.508 --> 00:16:21.702
Did he ever make any comments

00:16:21.743 --> 00:16:23.506
that might, in retrospect,
be suspicious?

00:16:23.545 --> 00:16:24.944
Not really.

00:16:24.979 --> 00:16:26.412
He hardly ever talked.

00:16:26.447 --> 00:16:29.416
Did you ever see him
outside Sick Bay?

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:32.817
Once or twice in Ten-Forward
with a group of people

00:16:32.854 --> 00:16:35.948
but I never had
a conversation with him.

00:16:36.057 --> 00:16:37.456
Thank you, Mr. Tarses.

00:16:37.492 --> 00:16:40.461
I don't think there's
need for more, Captain.

00:16:40.495 --> 00:16:42.087
You're excused, Crewman.

00:16:46.868 --> 00:16:48.199
Mr. Worf...

00:16:48.236 --> 00:16:49.396
Wait.

00:16:49.437 --> 00:16:51.098
He's lying.

00:16:51.139 --> 00:16:52.367
He's desperately frightened.

00:16:52.407 --> 00:16:53.533
He's covering something.

00:16:53.575 --> 00:16:55.338
It's clear that he's frightened

00:16:55.376 --> 00:16:56.866
but that's hardly
an indication...

00:16:56.911 --> 00:16:57.969
It's more than that.

00:16:58.046 --> 00:17:00.105
He wasn't truthful.

00:17:00.148 --> 00:17:01.274
He's covering a lie...

00:17:01.316 --> 00:17:03.841
one so big,
it's overwhelming him.

00:17:05.286 --> 00:17:07.311
I think we found the man.

00:17:20.535 --> 00:17:21.695
Admiral.

00:17:25.807 --> 00:17:27.604
I have to tell you

00:17:27.642 --> 00:17:30.270
you must not expect me
to permit any action

00:17:30.311 --> 00:17:34.611
against Mr. Tarses solely on
the basis of Betazoid intuition.

00:17:34.649 --> 00:17:36.742
Sabin has uncanny instincts.

00:17:36.784 --> 00:17:38.877
I've learned to trust them.

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:41.388
I'm not happy
about this use of a Betazoid.

00:17:41.422 --> 00:17:43.617
But you have
a Betazoid Counselor.

00:17:43.658 --> 00:17:46.126
Surely you're aware
of the advantages.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:48.060
But there is a difference

00:17:48.096 --> 00:17:51.122
between a Counselor
and an investigator.

00:17:51.165 --> 00:17:53.793
Are you saying you
never use your Counselor

00:17:53.835 --> 00:17:55.200
during interrogations?

00:17:56.738 --> 00:17:59.206
Yes, I do...

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:03.870
but I would not act solely
on the basis of her instinct.

00:18:05.313 --> 00:18:06.780
Nor do I.

00:18:06.814 --> 00:18:08.281
But you're asking...

00:18:10.118 --> 00:18:13.451
You're asking me to restrict
Mr. Tarses's movements

00:18:13.488 --> 00:18:16.013
solely on the basis
of Sabin's feeling.

00:18:16.057 --> 00:18:19.026
If Counselor Troi
suggested to you

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:22.029
that someone on this ship
were dangerous

00:18:22.063 --> 00:18:24.156
would you not act on that?

00:18:24.198 --> 00:18:27.190
Observe him, curb his activity?

00:18:28.703 --> 00:18:31.672
Yes, I admit I probably would

00:18:31.706 --> 00:18:34.800
and perhaps I should reevaluate
that behavior.

00:18:34.842 --> 00:18:36.139
Oh, nonsense.

00:18:36.177 --> 00:18:38.145
Let's keep our priorities
straight.

00:18:38.179 --> 00:18:39.646
The important thing

00:18:39.681 --> 00:18:41.945
is to uncover the conspiracy
on this ship

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:43.950
and to prevent further damage.

00:18:43.985 --> 00:18:46.613
Now, if Tarses
is a possible saboteur

00:18:46.654 --> 00:18:50.181
you cannot allow him access
to sensitive areas of this ship

00:18:50.224 --> 00:18:53.682
and I strongly suggest
continuous surveillance.

00:19:01.436 --> 00:19:03.563
If we had clear evidence...

00:19:03.604 --> 00:19:05.572
We will have clear evidence.

00:19:05.606 --> 00:19:08.541
Sabin and Lieutenant Worf
are continuing to investigate

00:19:08.576 --> 00:19:12.137
but if you don't act until then,
it may be too late.

00:19:16.384 --> 00:19:18.909
No.

00:19:18.953 --> 00:19:20.818
I won't treat a man
as a criminal

00:19:20.855 --> 00:19:22.686
unless there is cause to do so.

00:19:22.724 --> 00:19:25.352
And while you're being
so generous

00:19:25.393 --> 00:19:28.328
you give a saboteur a chance
to strike again?

00:19:28.362 --> 00:19:31.229
Last time, it was just
a hatch cover.

00:19:31.265 --> 00:19:33.665
What if next time
it's more serious?

00:19:33.701 --> 00:19:35.293
What if lives are lost?

00:19:35.336 --> 00:19:37.133
Can you afford not to act?

00:19:37.171 --> 00:19:39.571
Engineering to Captain Picard.

00:19:39.607 --> 00:19:41.165
Yes, Mr. La Forge?

00:19:41.209 --> 00:19:43.677
Captain, could you come
to Engineering right away?

00:19:43.711 --> 00:19:46.077
We've got something interesting
to show you.

00:19:46.114 --> 00:19:48.048
We'll be right there.

00:19:50.051 --> 00:19:53.214
Captain, we finally got in here
about six hours ago

00:19:53.254 --> 00:19:56.052
and we've been going over
it inch by inch ever since.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.285
We have made
microtomographic analyses

00:19:58.326 --> 00:20:00.590
of the dilithium chamber,
the hatch mounting

00:20:00.628 --> 00:20:02.459
the blast pattern
from the explosion.

00:20:02.497 --> 00:20:04.364
We did mass spectrometer
readings of the residue

00:20:04.497 --> 00:20:05.589
for chemical content

00:20:05.631 --> 00:20:08.099
sifted through the debris
for bomb fragments.

00:20:08.134 --> 00:20:09.431
What did you find?

00:20:09.469 --> 00:20:12.302
This is the frame for the hatch.

00:20:12.338 --> 00:20:14.704
It ruptured right along here

00:20:14.741 --> 00:20:18.336
and when we take a reading
of that spot...

00:20:19.412 --> 00:20:20.538
See?

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:23.743
I'm afraid I'm out
of my element, Commander.

00:20:23.783 --> 00:20:25.648
You'll have to interpret
for me.

00:20:25.685 --> 00:20:28.654
There are sub-micron fractures
in the metal casing.

00:20:28.688 --> 00:20:29.712
That's right.

00:20:29.756 --> 00:20:32.316
A breakdown of the atomic
cohesive structure.

00:20:32.358 --> 00:20:33.985
Yes, and what caused them?

00:20:34.026 --> 00:20:35.994
Those fractures
suggest nothing more

00:20:36.028 --> 00:20:37.586
than simple neutron fatigue.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:40.997
I would speculate that when
the engine was last inspected

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:44.092
at McKinley Station,
the hatch casing was replaced

00:20:44.137 --> 00:20:46.662
with one which had
an undetectable defect.

00:20:46.706 --> 00:20:47.866
I believe, sir

00:20:47.907 --> 00:20:49.807
that the conclusion
to our investigation

00:20:49.842 --> 00:20:52.538
must be that the explosion
was not intentional.

00:20:52.578 --> 00:20:54.205
That's the way I see it.

00:20:54.247 --> 00:20:56.215
This wasn't sabotage at all.

00:20:56.249 --> 00:20:58.774
It was nothing more than...
an accident.

00:21:02.622 --> 00:21:03.953
An accident?

00:21:05.625 --> 00:21:07.752
I find that hard to believe.

00:21:07.794 --> 00:21:10.592
If my crew say
there was no sabotage

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:12.598
you can be sure there was none.

00:21:12.632 --> 00:21:14.156
Let us keep our perspective,
gentlemen.

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:16.600
Just because
there was no sabotage

00:21:16.636 --> 00:21:19.196
doesn't mean there isn't
a conspiracy on this ship.

00:21:19.238 --> 00:21:21.069
We do have a confessed spy.

00:21:21.107 --> 00:21:23.132
And he had confederates.

00:21:23.176 --> 00:21:24.268
Do we know that for sure?

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:25.368
Of course he did.

00:21:25.411 --> 00:21:26.605
Do you think J'Dan

00:21:26.646 --> 00:21:29.342
could have come on board
the flagship of the Federation

00:21:29.382 --> 00:21:32.112
and accomplished what he did
without help from within?

00:21:34.153 --> 00:21:36.621
I agree it would be difficult...

00:21:36.656 --> 00:21:38.624
but not impossible.

00:21:38.658 --> 00:21:41.627
We should continue
to investigate Tarses.

00:21:41.661 --> 00:21:44.653
He was hiding something.

00:21:44.697 --> 00:21:46.494
Captain Picard,
Lieutenant Worf and I

00:21:46.532 --> 00:21:47.999
have been working well together.

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:50.364
I suggest we continue,
if for no other purpose

00:21:50.403 --> 00:21:52.234
than to determine
Tarses's innocence.

00:21:52.271 --> 00:21:55.206
Now, please, let me remind you
he is innocent

00:21:55.241 --> 00:21:57.004
until he is proved guilty.

00:21:57.043 --> 00:21:58.670
Of course he is.

00:21:58.711 --> 00:22:01.942
What Sabin is saying
is that he and Lieutenant Worf

00:22:01.981 --> 00:22:04.347
would like to establish
his innocence

00:22:04.383 --> 00:22:06.544
unequivocally, for his own sake.

00:22:07.954 --> 00:22:12.220
Very well, but let us put this
to rest as quickly as possible.

00:22:29.709 --> 00:22:32.177
You've opened the hearing
to spectators?

00:22:32.211 --> 00:22:35.180
It isn't good to have
closed-door proceedings

00:22:35.214 --> 00:22:36.181
for too long.

00:22:36.215 --> 00:22:38.115
It invites rumor
and speculation.

00:22:38.150 --> 00:22:40.209
Nevertheless, Admiral,
I think it would be wise...

00:22:40.253 --> 00:22:41.515
Because spies and saboteurs

00:22:41.554 --> 00:22:44.990
don't like the bright lights
of an open inquiry.

00:22:45.024 --> 00:22:48.482
They're like roaches,
scurrying for the dark corner.

00:22:55.101 --> 00:22:59.094
This hearing is convened
on Stardate 44780

00:22:59.138 --> 00:23:01.106
as a continuing inquiry

00:23:01.140 --> 00:23:04.871
into the activities
of Crewman Simon Tarses.

00:23:04.911 --> 00:23:06.936
Mr. Tarses,
for your own protection

00:23:07.046 --> 00:23:09.139
I have assigned a counsel to you

00:23:09.181 --> 00:23:11.342
in the person
of Commander William Riker.

00:23:11.384 --> 00:23:13.716
Thank you, sir,
but I don't need protection.

00:23:13.753 --> 00:23:15.550
I have not done anything wrong.

00:23:15.588 --> 00:23:20.958
Dr. Crusher, have you observed
Crewman Tarses with J'Dan?

00:23:21.060 --> 00:23:24.621
Well, yes, he gave him
his injection.

00:23:24.664 --> 00:23:26.928
I meant outside of Sick Bay.

00:23:29.135 --> 00:23:31.103
I think so.

00:23:31.137 --> 00:23:32.468
Perhaps in Ten-Forward.

00:23:32.505 --> 00:23:35.963
And whom else have you observed
at these occasions?

00:23:36.008 --> 00:23:38.602
I don't understand
what relevance that has.

00:23:38.644 --> 00:23:40.771
It was an innocent
social gathering.

00:23:40.813 --> 00:23:42.781
If it was so innocent

00:23:42.815 --> 00:23:45.875
why do you hesitate
to give us the names?

00:23:45.918 --> 00:23:47.749
Thank you, Doctor.

00:23:47.787 --> 00:23:51.484
Admiral, if you have a case
to make against Simon Tarses

00:23:51.524 --> 00:23:52.718
you had better make it.

00:23:52.758 --> 00:23:55.022
Otherwise, I'm stopping
this here and now.

00:24:01.968 --> 00:24:06.428
Mr. Tarses, isn't it true
that you have access

00:24:06.472 --> 00:24:08.804
to the biological
supplies in Sick Bay?

00:24:08.841 --> 00:24:10.308
It's part of my job, yes.

00:24:10.343 --> 00:24:12.641
J'Dan used suspensions
of deoxyribose

00:24:12.678 --> 00:24:14.646
to carry the encoded files
he stole.

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:17.945
Isn't it true one of your duties
is to prepare these suspensions?

00:24:18.017 --> 00:24:19.746
Several technicians
share that job.

00:24:19.785 --> 00:24:21.753
And isn't it true
that your security clearance

00:24:21.787 --> 00:24:24.950
allow you access to all
the stores and files in Sick Bay

00:24:25.024 --> 00:24:27.151
access which you can exercise
at any time?

00:24:27.193 --> 00:24:29.218
Because I have access
does not mean I...

00:24:29.261 --> 00:24:32.458
What would you say if I told you
there is evidence

00:24:32.498 --> 00:24:34.090
that the explosion
in the engine room was caused

00:24:34.133 --> 00:24:35.122
by a corrosive chemical...

00:24:35.167 --> 00:24:38.534
one that is kept
stored in Sick Bay?

00:24:38.571 --> 00:24:40.766
I had nothing to do with that.

00:24:40.806 --> 00:24:42.774
How can we believe you?

00:24:42.808 --> 00:24:45.402
How can we believe someone
whom we know...

00:24:45.444 --> 00:24:47.412
we know to be a liar?

00:24:47.446 --> 00:24:48.572
I object.

00:24:48.614 --> 00:24:50.844
There is no basis for calling
Crewman Tarses a liar.

00:24:50.883 --> 00:24:51.975
Agreed. Mr. Sabin.

00:24:52.051 --> 00:24:53.348
Captain, there is a basis

00:24:53.386 --> 00:24:55.854
which will become clear
in a moment.

00:24:55.888 --> 00:24:56.912
Mr. Tarses, didn't you

00:24:56.956 --> 00:24:58.651
deliberately
and premeditatively lie

00:24:58.691 --> 00:25:00.921
when you filled out
your personnel application

00:25:00.960 --> 00:25:04.054
and compounded that lie by
repeating it to this committee?

00:25:04.096 --> 00:25:05.063
What?

00:25:05.097 --> 00:25:06.394
Isn't it true

00:25:06.432 --> 00:25:08.923
that the paternal grandfather
of whom you speak

00:25:09.001 --> 00:25:11.526
was not a Vulcan, but was,
in fact, a Romulan?

00:25:11.570 --> 00:25:14.539
That it is Romulan blood
you carry

00:25:14.573 --> 00:25:17.599
and a Romulan heritage
that you honor?

00:25:17.643 --> 00:25:20.476
We're waiting, Mr. Tarses.

00:25:20.513 --> 00:25:23.482
On the advice of my counsel

00:25:23.516 --> 00:25:28.351
I refuse to answer
that question in...

00:25:28.387 --> 00:25:30.855
in that the answer m...

00:25:30.890 --> 00:25:33.586
might serve to incriminate me.

00:25:52.478 --> 00:25:54.173
You and Crewman Marcus
will coordinate

00:25:54.213 --> 00:25:57.842
to track Tarses's movements
over the last five years.

00:25:57.883 --> 00:26:00.909
Ensign Kellogg, I want a list
of all relatives

00:26:00.953 --> 00:26:04.320
known associates and especially
old school friends

00:26:04.356 --> 00:26:05.380
and make arrangements

00:26:05.424 --> 00:26:07.858
to do an encephalographic
polygraph scan...

00:26:07.893 --> 00:26:09.758
Mr. Worf.

00:26:09.795 --> 00:26:11.786
Yes, Captain?

00:26:11.831 --> 00:26:14.163
I need to speak with you.

00:26:15.735 --> 00:26:16.861
You are dismissed.

00:26:16.902 --> 00:26:19.234
Please get your reports to me
as soon as possible.

00:26:30.216 --> 00:26:32.548
Do you see what is
happening here, Mr. Worf?

00:26:34.587 --> 00:26:35.884
Sir?

00:26:35.921 --> 00:26:38.355
This is not unlike a...

00:26:38.390 --> 00:26:40.790
a drumhead trial.

00:26:42.962 --> 00:26:44.827
I do not understand.

00:26:46.665 --> 00:26:48.826
500 years ago, military officers

00:26:48.868 --> 00:26:51.393
would upend a drum
on the battlefield.

00:26:51.437 --> 00:26:53.530
They'd sit at it
and dispense summary justice.

00:26:53.572 --> 00:26:55.437
Decisions were quick,
punishments severe

00:26:55.474 --> 00:26:58.102
appeals denied.

00:26:58.144 --> 00:27:01.238
Those who came to a drumhead
were doomed.

00:27:01.280 --> 00:27:04.078
But we know
there is a traitor here.

00:27:04.116 --> 00:27:06.818
J'Dan has admitted his guilt.

00:27:06.951 --> 00:27:08.919
That's true, and he will stand
for his crime.

00:27:09.020 --> 00:27:11.011
Tarses has all but done
the same.

00:27:11.055 --> 00:27:12.022
How?

00:27:12.056 --> 00:27:13.614
He refused to answer
the question

00:27:13.658 --> 00:27:15.421
about his Romulan grandfather.

00:27:15.459 --> 00:27:17.086
That is not a crime, Worf!

00:27:18.529 --> 00:27:21.794
Nor can we infer his guilt
because he didn't respond.

00:27:21.833 --> 00:27:26.361
Sir, if a man were not afraid
of the truth, he would answer.

00:27:26.404 --> 00:27:28.133
Oh, no.

00:27:28.172 --> 00:27:32.268
We cannot allow ourselves
to think that.

00:27:32.310 --> 00:27:35.541
The Seventh Guarantee is one
of the most important rights

00:27:35.580 --> 00:27:37.138
granted by the Federation.

00:27:37.181 --> 00:27:39.547
We cannot take
a fundamental principle

00:27:39.584 --> 00:27:43.452
of the Constitution
and turn it against a citizen.

00:27:43.487 --> 00:27:46.923
Sir, the Federation does
have enemies.

00:27:46.958 --> 00:27:49.392
We must seek them out.

00:27:51.162 --> 00:27:52.527
Oh, yes.

00:27:54.031 --> 00:27:56.795
That's how it starts

00:27:56.834 --> 00:27:59.735
but the road
from legitimate suspicion

00:27:59.770 --> 00:28:04.036
to rampant paranoia is very much
shorter than we think.

00:28:04.075 --> 00:28:06.305
Something is wrong here,
Mr. Worf.

00:28:06.344 --> 00:28:08.369
I don't like
what we have become.

00:28:19.957 --> 00:28:22.016
There you are, Mr. Tarses.

00:28:22.059 --> 00:28:24.050
Would you care for some lemon?

00:28:24.095 --> 00:28:26.222
No, thank you, sir,
this is fine.

00:28:26.264 --> 00:28:29.358
Well, tell me a little
about yourself, Crewman.

00:28:29.400 --> 00:28:32.028
I know you were born
on Mars Colony.

00:28:32.069 --> 00:28:33.559
Yes, sir.

00:28:35.439 --> 00:28:38.237
All my life, I wanted
to be in Starfleet.

00:28:38.276 --> 00:28:43.339
I went to the Academy's training
program for enlisted personnel.

00:28:43.381 --> 00:28:44.939
I took training
as a medical technician

00:28:44.982 --> 00:28:47.849
and I served
at several outposts.

00:28:47.885 --> 00:28:50.376
The day that I was posted
to the Enterprise

00:28:50.421 --> 00:28:52.286
was the happiest day of my life.

00:28:52.323 --> 00:28:54.086
Did you ever consider
applying to the Academy

00:28:54.125 --> 00:28:55.149
going the whole route?

00:28:55.192 --> 00:28:57.660
Apply to become an officer?

00:28:57.695 --> 00:29:01.893
Well, my parents wanted me
to, and I thought about it.

00:29:01.933 --> 00:29:05.266
I used to sit
under this big tree

00:29:05.303 --> 00:29:06.770
near the parade grounds.

00:29:06.804 --> 00:29:09.364
An elm tree
with a circular bench?

00:29:09.407 --> 00:29:10.374
Yes, that's the one.

00:29:10.408 --> 00:29:11.670
I spent many an hour there.

00:29:11.709 --> 00:29:13.301
It was my favorite spot
to study.

00:29:15.012 --> 00:29:19.346
I used to sit under that tree
and watch the drills.

00:29:19.383 --> 00:29:22.580
Picture myself an officer.

00:29:22.620 --> 00:29:27.614
I know that it would have made
my mother very happy, but I...

00:29:27.658 --> 00:29:29.523
You didn't do it.

00:29:29.560 --> 00:29:30.527
No.

00:29:30.561 --> 00:29:35.191
I was 18 and eager.

00:29:35.232 --> 00:29:39.134
The last thing I wanted
was to spend four years

00:29:39.170 --> 00:29:41.035
sitting in classrooms.

00:29:41.072 --> 00:29:46.908
I wanted to be out there,
traveling the stars.

00:29:46.944 --> 00:29:50.311
I didn't want to wait
for anything.

00:29:53.317 --> 00:29:55.410
And now it's done, isn't it?

00:29:55.453 --> 00:29:58.581
My career in Starfleet
is finished.

00:29:58.622 --> 00:30:02.217
Not if you aren't guilty, Simon.

00:30:02.259 --> 00:30:05.251
It doesn't matter.

00:30:05.296 --> 00:30:07.264
I lied on my application.

00:30:10.167 --> 00:30:13.500
And that mistake will be with me
for the rest of my life.

00:30:20.878 --> 00:30:24.507
Mr. Worf has found a brother
who still lives on Mars Colony.

00:30:24.548 --> 00:30:26.516
Contact someone there
and have him interviewed.

00:30:26.550 --> 00:30:27.517
Admiral Satie...

00:30:27.551 --> 00:30:28.813
And start a background checkup

00:30:28.853 --> 00:30:30.980
into all his friends
at the Academy training program.

00:30:31.022 --> 00:30:31.989
Admiral Satie?

00:30:32.089 --> 00:30:32.987
Yes, Captain?

00:30:33.090 --> 00:30:34.318
I would like
to have a word with you.

00:30:34.358 --> 00:30:35.484
Of course.

00:30:35.526 --> 00:30:37.551
In private...

00:30:37.595 --> 00:30:39.392
and off the record.

00:30:40.531 --> 00:30:42.294
Of course.

00:30:42.333 --> 00:30:44.528
After all,
you are my partner in this.

00:30:48.739 --> 00:30:51.003
I cannot possibly believe
you'd mean this.

00:30:51.075 --> 00:30:52.201
But I do.

00:30:52.243 --> 00:30:53.437
This must stop.

00:30:53.477 --> 00:30:54.739
It has gone too far.

00:30:54.779 --> 00:30:56.542
You lied to him
about the engine room.

00:30:56.580 --> 00:30:59.105
There were no volatile chemicals
found there.

00:30:59.150 --> 00:31:02.210
It was a tactic...
a way of applying pressure.

00:31:02.253 --> 00:31:06.212
We're hounding an innocent man.

00:31:06.257 --> 00:31:08.953
And how, may I ask, have you
managed to determine that?

00:31:08.993 --> 00:31:10.585
I've talked with him.

00:31:12.196 --> 00:31:13.891
Oh, I see.

00:31:13.931 --> 00:31:17.594
And he told you he was
a victim of circumstance...

00:31:17.635 --> 00:31:19.068
blameless and pure?

00:31:19.103 --> 00:31:20.400
No.

00:31:20.438 --> 00:31:23.601
He admits his mistake
in falsifying his application

00:31:23.641 --> 00:31:25.973
but that does not make him
a traitor.

00:31:28.746 --> 00:31:31.613
How can you be
so incredibly naive?

00:31:34.018 --> 00:31:36.077
Captain, may I tell you

00:31:36.120 --> 00:31:39.385
how I have spent
the past four years?

00:31:39.423 --> 00:31:42.392
From planet to Starbase
to planet.

00:31:42.426 --> 00:31:44.189
I have no home.

00:31:44.228 --> 00:31:47.493
I live on starships
and shuttlecraft.

00:31:47.531 --> 00:31:49.999
I haven't seen
a family member in years.

00:31:50.101 --> 00:31:55.505
I have no friends,
but I have a purpose.

00:31:55.539 --> 00:31:58.337
My father taught me from
the time I was a little girl

00:31:58.375 --> 00:32:00.240
still clutching a blanket

00:32:00.277 --> 00:32:02.802
that the United Federation
of Planets

00:32:02.847 --> 00:32:07.079
is the most remarkable
institution ever conceived

00:32:07.118 --> 00:32:10.554
and it is my cause to make sure

00:32:10.588 --> 00:32:13.921
that this extraordinary
union be preserved.

00:32:13.958 --> 00:32:16.552
I cannot imagine
why you are trying

00:32:16.594 --> 00:32:18.755
to block this investigation.

00:32:18.796 --> 00:32:21.731
There have been others
in the past who doubted me.

00:32:23.033 --> 00:32:24.660
They came to regret it.

00:32:32.109 --> 00:32:35.442
The hearings on Simon Tarses
will stop.

00:32:35.479 --> 00:32:37.811
If necessary,
I will go to Starfleet Command.

00:32:37.848 --> 00:32:40.578
I have news for you, Captain.

00:32:40.618 --> 00:32:44.213
I've been in constant contact
with Starfleet Command.

00:32:44.255 --> 00:32:46.985
The hearings
are not going to stop.

00:32:47.024 --> 00:32:48.514
They're going to be expanded.

00:32:48.559 --> 00:32:50.288
What are you saying?

00:32:50.327 --> 00:32:53.888
I'm going to get
to the heart of this conspiracy

00:32:53.931 --> 00:32:57.367
if it means investigating
every last person on this ship

00:32:57.401 --> 00:33:01.895
and every hearing from now on
will be held in the presence

00:33:01.939 --> 00:33:05.534
of Admiral Thomas Henry
of Starfleet Security.

00:33:05.576 --> 00:33:08.204
I've requested
he be brought here at once.

00:33:08.245 --> 00:33:10.440
You never told me about this.

00:33:10.481 --> 00:33:12.949
I report to Starfleet Command
directly.

00:33:13.050 --> 00:33:15.883
I do not need your permission
or your approval

00:33:15.920 --> 00:33:17.251
for my decisions.

00:33:19.590 --> 00:33:21.455
Admiral.

00:33:21.492 --> 00:33:23.551
What you're doing here...

00:33:23.594 --> 00:33:26.324
is unethical.

00:33:26.363 --> 00:33:27.921
It's immoral.

00:33:29.266 --> 00:33:31.461
I'll fight it.

00:33:31.502 --> 00:33:34.096
Do what you must, Captain.

00:33:35.606 --> 00:33:37.597
And so will I.

00:33:47.451 --> 00:33:50.579
Captain, warp engines
are back on line.

00:33:50.621 --> 00:33:53.215
We are ready to commence
restart sequences.

00:33:55.526 --> 00:33:56.925
Sir?

00:33:56.961 --> 00:33:58.519
Yes?

00:33:58.562 --> 00:34:01.224
Yes, yes, of course,
proceed, Mr. Data.

00:34:04.635 --> 00:34:06.660
You all right, Captain?

00:34:06.704 --> 00:34:10.105
Yes, of course, Number One,
just a little preoccupied.

00:34:12.775 --> 00:34:14.902
Admiral Satie has ordered you
to report

00:34:14.944 --> 00:34:19.074
to the interrogation room
at 0900 hours tomorrow morning.

00:34:19.115 --> 00:34:21.879
You are to be questioned
before the committee.

00:34:35.264 --> 00:34:37.232
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:34:37.266 --> 00:34:38.927
Admiral Thomas Henry

00:34:38.968 --> 00:34:41.493
who has worked closely
with Norah Satie in the past

00:34:41.537 --> 00:34:44.131
has arrived
to observe the hearings.

00:34:46.075 --> 00:34:47.099
Your full name?

00:34:47.143 --> 00:34:48.610
Jean-Luc Picard.

00:34:48.644 --> 00:34:49.736
Rank and position?

00:34:49.779 --> 00:34:51.770
Captain,
Federation Starship Enterprise.

00:34:51.814 --> 00:34:53.304
How long have you
held this post?

00:34:53.349 --> 00:34:56.648
Over three years,
since Stardate 41124.

00:34:56.686 --> 00:34:58.916
Very well. Admiral.

00:34:58.954 --> 00:35:01.286
If you don't mind, there is
something I would like to say.

00:35:01.323 --> 00:35:03.917
If you have a statement,
you'll have an opportunity

00:35:03.959 --> 00:35:05.517
to make it later.

00:35:05.561 --> 00:35:07.119
I believe that Chapter Four

00:35:07.163 --> 00:35:09.256
Article 12
of the Uniform Code of Justice

00:35:09.298 --> 00:35:11.323
grants me the right
to make a statement

00:35:11.367 --> 00:35:13.801
before questioning begins.

00:35:13.836 --> 00:35:15.269
Very well.

00:35:18.307 --> 00:35:21.071
I'm deeply concerned
about what is happening here.

00:35:22.511 --> 00:35:26.948
It began
when we apprehended a spy...

00:35:27.016 --> 00:35:28.643
a man who admitted his guilt

00:35:28.684 --> 00:35:30.652
and who will answer
for his crime.

00:35:30.686 --> 00:35:34.053
But the hunt didn't end there.

00:35:34.090 --> 00:35:38.049
Another man, Mr. Simon Tarses,
was brought to trial...

00:35:38.094 --> 00:35:43.327
and it was a trial, no matter
what others choose to call it.

00:35:43.365 --> 00:35:49.235
A trial based on insinuation
and innuendo.

00:35:49.271 --> 00:35:52.900
Nothing substantive
offered against Mr. Tarses

00:35:52.942 --> 00:35:54.307
much less proven.

00:35:57.346 --> 00:36:01.749
Mr. Tarses's grandfather
is Romulan

00:36:01.784 --> 00:36:07.086
and for that reason,
his career now stands in ruins.

00:36:08.991 --> 00:36:13.018
Have we become so... fearful

00:36:13.062 --> 00:36:16.793
have we become so cowardly

00:36:16.832 --> 00:36:21.269
that we must extinguish a man

00:36:21.303 --> 00:36:24.602
because he carries the blood
of a current enemy?

00:36:24.640 --> 00:36:27.609
Admiral...

00:36:27.643 --> 00:36:32.945
let us not condemn Simon Tarses
or anyone else

00:36:33.015 --> 00:36:35.347
because of their bloodlines

00:36:35.384 --> 00:36:40.253
or investigate others
for their innocent associations.

00:36:40.289 --> 00:36:42.120
I implore you.

00:36:42.158 --> 00:36:47.425
Do not continue
with this... proceeding.

00:36:47.463 --> 00:36:49.727
End it now.

00:36:51.433 --> 00:36:54.402
Captain, do you believe
in the Prime Directive?

00:36:54.436 --> 00:36:55.460
Of course.

00:36:55.504 --> 00:36:57.062
In fact, it's Starfleet's

00:36:57.106 --> 00:36:59.973
General Order Number One,
is it not?

00:37:00.042 --> 00:37:01.100
Your point, Admiral?

00:37:01.143 --> 00:37:02.804
Would it surprise you to learn

00:37:02.845 --> 00:37:05.109
that you have violated
the Prime Directive

00:37:05.147 --> 00:37:08.344
a total of nine times
since you took command

00:37:08.384 --> 00:37:09.578
of the Enterprise?

00:37:09.618 --> 00:37:12.781
I must say, Captain, it
surprised the hell out of me.

00:37:12.822 --> 00:37:14.915
My reports to Starfleet

00:37:14.957 --> 00:37:17.721
will document the circumstances
of those instances.

00:37:17.760 --> 00:37:20.388
Yes, we're looking into
those reports, Captain...

00:37:20.429 --> 00:37:22.329
very closely into those reports.

00:37:22.364 --> 00:37:26.232
After which, I'm sure we'll have
more questions for you

00:37:26.268 --> 00:37:28.634
about your so-called
commitment

00:37:28.671 --> 00:37:30.195
to Starfleet Prime Directive.

00:37:34.276 --> 00:37:36.141
Captain, could you tell us

00:37:36.178 --> 00:37:40.080
just what happened
on Stardate 44390?

00:37:40.115 --> 00:37:41.844
I beg your pardon?

00:37:41.884 --> 00:37:43.943
Let me refresh your memory.

00:37:43.986 --> 00:37:48.480
You were transporting
a Vulcan ambassador... T'Pel.

00:37:48.524 --> 00:37:55.123
I was following orders
to... take this ambassador

00:37:55.164 --> 00:37:56.961
to a location
near the Neutral Zone.

00:37:57.032 --> 00:37:58.693
I don't think
we need the preamble.

00:37:58.734 --> 00:38:02.693
In fact, she was not a Vulcan
at all, was she?

00:38:02.738 --> 00:38:04.171
She was a Romulan spy.

00:38:06.542 --> 00:38:07.702
That's correct.

00:38:07.743 --> 00:38:09.438
A spy whom you were delivering

00:38:09.478 --> 00:38:11.309
back into the hands
of the enemy.

00:38:11.347 --> 00:38:14.214
Tell me, Captain,
when the deception was revealed

00:38:14.250 --> 00:38:17.310
and she stood proudly
on the Bridge of a Romulan ship

00:38:17.353 --> 00:38:20.117
did you make any effort
to retrieve her?

00:38:20.155 --> 00:38:22.680
- No.
- No.

00:38:22.725 --> 00:38:26.627
Even though you knew
she carried Federation secrets

00:38:26.662 --> 00:38:28.789
that she had been
accumulating for years?

00:38:28.831 --> 00:38:33.564
The Enterprise could have been
captured by the Romulans.

00:38:33.602 --> 00:38:35.934
Captain Picard did
the only thing he could.

00:38:36.005 --> 00:38:37.495
Really, Lieutenant.

00:38:37.539 --> 00:38:39.530
And where were you
when this traitor

00:38:39.575 --> 00:38:41.543
was on board the Enterprise?

00:38:41.577 --> 00:38:43.067
Where was ship's security?

00:38:43.112 --> 00:38:45.239
Don't you think
it's questionable judgment

00:38:45.281 --> 00:38:46.839
Captain, to have
a security officer

00:38:46.882 --> 00:38:48.816
whose father was
a Romulan collaborator?

00:38:49.985 --> 00:38:51.213
Lieutenant.

00:39:02.231 --> 00:39:04.062
Tell me, Captain.

00:39:04.099 --> 00:39:06.590
Have you completely recovered

00:39:06.635 --> 00:39:09.001
from your experience
with the Borg?

00:39:10.706 --> 00:39:13.436
Yes, I have
completely recovered.

00:39:13.475 --> 00:39:17.172
It must have been awful for you

00:39:17.212 --> 00:39:19.840
actually becoming one of them

00:39:19.882 --> 00:39:22.646
being forced to use
your vast knowledge

00:39:22.685 --> 00:39:26.348
of Starfleet operations
to aid the Borg.

00:39:26.388 --> 00:39:29.721
Just how many
of our ships were lost?

00:39:29.758 --> 00:39:31.919
Thirty-nine?

00:39:31.961 --> 00:39:37.399
And a loss of life, I believe,
measured at nearly 11,000.

00:39:37.433 --> 00:39:41.460
One wonders
how you can sleep at night

00:39:41.503 --> 00:39:43.937
having caused
so much destruction.

00:39:44.039 --> 00:39:46.473
I question your actions,
Captain.

00:39:46.508 --> 00:39:48.305
I question your choices.

00:39:48.344 --> 00:39:51.006
I question your Ioyalty.

00:39:52.715 --> 00:39:55.684
You know, there are
some words I've known

00:39:55.718 --> 00:39:57.481
since I was a schoolboy.

00:39:57.519 --> 00:40:00.955
"With the first link,
the chain is forged.

00:40:01.023 --> 00:40:03.617
"The first speech censured

00:40:03.659 --> 00:40:05.627
"the first thought forbidden

00:40:05.661 --> 00:40:07.686
"the first freedom denied

00:40:07.730 --> 00:40:09.994
chains us all irrevocably."

00:40:12.167 --> 00:40:15.967
Those words were uttered
by Judge Aaron Satie

00:40:16.038 --> 00:40:20.975
as wisdom and warning.

00:40:21.043 --> 00:40:26.071
The first time any man's freedom
is trodden on

00:40:26.115 --> 00:40:28.310
we are all damaged.

00:40:28.350 --> 00:40:29.977
I fear that today...

00:40:30.085 --> 00:40:31.245
How dare you...

00:40:31.286 --> 00:40:35.245
you who consort with Romulans...

00:40:35.290 --> 00:40:37.258
invoke my father's name

00:40:37.292 --> 00:40:40.489
to support
your traitorous arguments?!

00:40:40.529 --> 00:40:43.828
It is an offense
to everything I hold dear!

00:40:43.866 --> 00:40:46.926
And to hear those words
used to subvert

00:40:46.969 --> 00:40:49.199
the United Federation
of Planets.

00:40:49.238 --> 00:40:52.002
My father was a great man.

00:40:52.074 --> 00:40:55.840
His name stands
for integrity and principle.

00:40:55.878 --> 00:41:00.008
You dirty his name
when you speak it.

00:41:00.082 --> 00:41:02.050
He loved the Federation

00:41:02.084 --> 00:41:04.382
but you, Captain, corrupt it.

00:41:04.420 --> 00:41:07.480
You undermine
our very way of life.

00:41:07.523 --> 00:41:09.324
I will expose you
for what you are.

00:41:09.324 --> 00:41:10.882
I will expose you
for what you are.

00:41:10.925 --> 00:41:15.362
I've brought down
bigger men than you, Picard!

00:41:39.287 --> 00:41:41.687
I have nothing more to say.

00:41:51.299 --> 00:41:55.998
Perhaps we should
call a recess until tomorrow.

00:42:38.179 --> 00:42:40.545
Am I bothering you, Captain?

00:42:40.581 --> 00:42:42.913
No, please, Mr. Worf, come in.

00:42:52.794 --> 00:42:54.955
It is over.

00:42:54.996 --> 00:42:57.157
Admiral Henry has called an end

00:42:57.198 --> 00:42:59.996
to any more hearings
on this matter.

00:43:00.034 --> 00:43:01.524
That's good.

00:43:03.971 --> 00:43:07.839
Admiral Satie has
left the Enterprise.

00:43:12.814 --> 00:43:15.282
We think we've come so far.

00:43:15.316 --> 00:43:19.150
Torture of heretics,
burning of witches

00:43:19.187 --> 00:43:21.451
is all ancient history.

00:43:21.489 --> 00:43:25.448
Then, before you
can blink an eye

00:43:25.493 --> 00:43:29.361
suddenly, it threatens
to start all over again.

00:43:31.933 --> 00:43:34.231
I believed her.

00:43:34.268 --> 00:43:37.465
I... I helped her.

00:43:37.505 --> 00:43:41.908
I did not see what she was.

00:43:41.943 --> 00:43:45.572
Mr. Worf, villains
who twirl their mustaches

00:43:45.613 --> 00:43:46.978
are easy to spot.

00:43:47.081 --> 00:43:49.845
Those who clothe themselves
in good deeds

00:43:49.884 --> 00:43:51.647
are well-camouflaged.

00:43:51.686 --> 00:43:55.713
I think... after yesterday

00:43:55.756 --> 00:43:59.852
people will not be
so ready to trust her.

00:43:59.894 --> 00:44:02.260
Maybe.

00:44:02.296 --> 00:44:05.663
But she, or someone like her,
will always be with us

00:44:05.700 --> 00:44:08.533
waiting for the right climate
in which to flourish

00:44:08.569 --> 00:44:12.699
spreading fear
in the name of righteousness.

00:44:16.976 --> 00:44:20.173
Vigilance, Mr. Worf.

00:44:20.213 --> 00:44:22.613
That is the price
we have to continually pay.
